ote; or (2) provides that the assignment or transfer or the creation, at- tachment, perfection, or enforcement of the security interest may give rise to a default, breach, right of recoupment, claim, defense, termina- tion, right of termination, or remedy under the account, chattel paper, payment intangible, or promissory note. (e) [Inapplicability of subsection (d) to certain sales.] Subsec- tion (d) does not apply to the sale of a payment intangible or promissory note, other than a sale pursuant to a disposition under Section 9–610 or an acceptance of collateral under Section 9–620. § 9–406 UNIFORM COMMERCIAL CODE"